  "caveats": [
    "Under the strict key every cohort contains exactly two metals, so the five-metal ranking is only ever observed in two of its five positions.",
    "The additive arm is separable: prediction = f(ligand) + g(metal) + h(cell), so its within-cohort metal order is one global order per fold (see additive_ranking_invariance). It can only beat global_best by estimating that single order better than the raw fold mean does.",
    "The loose key pools up to 18 distinct canonical compounds into one cohort; its deltas are confounded by compound identity and are a sensitivity check, not the primary result.",
    "Baselines are fold-safe but still estimated from the same corpus that supplies the evaluation cohorts; a genuinely prospective test would need held-out papers.",
    "The model's counterfactual five-metal picks are scored only where the pick happens to have been measured, a subset chosen by the model itself."
  ]
}
